lesson: 218
title: Fence around a square
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: A square has 4 sides, and all 4 sides are the same length.
explain: To go all the way around a square, walk along all 4 sides: the length around is 4 times one side.
explain: A square sandpit with a side of 3 metres needs 3 × 4 = 12 metres of fence to go all around it.
vars: a=name s=2..25 z=2..9
answer: s * 4
exercise: A square sandpit has sides of {s} metres. How many metres of fence go all the way around it?
exercise: {a}'s garden is a square with a side of {s} metres. How long is the fence around the garden?
exercise: A square rug measures {s} feet on each side. How many feet of ribbon are needed to edge it all around?
exercise: {a} walks once around a square field with sides of {s} metres. How many metres does {a.he} walk?
exercise: A square vegetable bed has a side of {s} metres. How many metres of edging go around it?
exercise: How long is the path around a square pond if one side of the pond is {s} metres?
exercise: square sandpit, {s} m a side. how much fence all round
exercise: our yard's square, {s} metres each side, dad wants fairy lights all round. how many metres
exercise: {a} says square {s} m a side needs {s*2} m of fence. nope. how many metres
exercise: the rug's square, {s+1} feet — no sorry {s} feet — a side. ribbon round the edge, how many feet
exercise: square chicken run {s} m a side, {z} chickens in it. fence all round = how many m
test: How many metres of fence enclose a square paddock whose side is {s} metres?
test: The edge of a square playground is {s} metres long on one side. {a} runs once around it. How far does {a.he} run?
test: Ribbon is glued all around a square card with {s} cm sides. How many centimetres of ribbon are used?
test: Around a square pool, {s} metres on a side, there is a fence. How long is the fence?
test: square patio {s} m one side, how many m round it
test: {z} plants inside a square bed with {s} m sides. how much edging round the outside
exam: A sandpit of square plan has a side length of {s} metres. Determine the length of fencing required to enclose it completely.
exam: Given that each side of a square plot measures {s.words} metres, ascertain its perimeter in metres.
exam: Compute the length of ribbon, in centimetres, necessary to border a square card of side {s} centimetres.
exam: It is stated that a pedestrian completes one circuit of a square field of side {s} metres. State the distance thus travelled.
exercise: The old fence "gave up the ghost" in the storm, every bit of it. The square paddock has sides of {s} metres. How many metres of new fence are needed to go all the way round?
exercise: the pony "went to live on a farm" so dad's turning the paddock into a veggie patch. it's square, {s} m a side, needs a fence all round. how many metres, quit stalling
test: The neighbour admits his figures were "not entirely accurate": the square lawn is not {s+2} metres a side but {s}. How many metres of edging go all the way round it?
